		{
			dependencies: ["7693869D7A33CBBE"]
			dependency_requirement: "one_completed"
			description: [
				"&aAll disks placed in the super disk array will be packaged as virtual disks for AE use &c&n(the array needs to be placed in the ME disk warehouse) &r, &aIn other words, you can stuff a bunch of infinite disks into the array and then put them into the disk warehouse. AE will read the internal disk content (the network to read the disk depends on the network you are connected to)"
				""
				"&m&l&cI do not recommend you to use SDA to store items (NBT has not been simplified for maximum compatibility). I have sent you a swallow disk. It is recommended that the swallow disk drive stores items with the highest priority. Beware of SDA nbt explosion!"
				""
				"&l&aAfter version 2.7.5, SDA has its own NBT optimization, using three layers of optimization: 1. Internal NBT simplification, 2. Serialized KEY hash optimization, 3. NBT is changed to external storage and is not stored in the SDA item body NBT, using UUID identification."
				"&l&cNote: You must install the SDA UUID identification file under /kubejs/data/sda_uuid_store/, otherwise the task SDA collection is directly a rolling log"
				""
				"&l&7View the introduction picture on the next page➡️⬇️"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"{image:dishanhai_item:textures/guis/dishanhai_1.png width:100 height:160 align:left fit:true}"
				"{image:dishanhai_item:textures/guis/dishanhai_2.png width:100 height:100 align:center fit:true}"
				"{image:dishanhai_item:textures/guis/dishanhai_3.png width:150 height:100 align:center fit:true}"
			]
