		{
			dependencies: ["7693869D7A33CBBE"]
			description: [
				"&e&lThe virtual item system is divided into two layers:"
				"&71. In the default configuration, the virtual item inspection channel directly acts on the AE inventory and does not require a virtual item supply machine. It is redundant."
				"&72. In another configuration, the virtual item inspection channel requires the corresponding items to be placed inside the virtual item supply machine. There are items in the network that cannot pass the inspection."
				""
				"&a&lNotes on virtual items (assertions):"
				"&71. For programming circuits, it is in the unwrapped configuration queue by default. If your programming circuit is still wrapped, you can open gt_shanhai's virtual item exclusion configuration and write the item ID of the programming circuit ( gtceu:programmed_circuit )"
				""
				"&72. Non-consumable items in the sample will actively check the original formula. After the system check is completed, the corresponding items will be wrapped as virtual item providers (and bound to the NBT of the corresponding items), but you do not need to specially prepare the corresponding virtual item providers, such as: vacuum tube virtual item providers. You only need to put a vacuum tube in the network, and the virtual items will allow verification and ordering."
				""
				"&73. Virtual items only participate in non-consumption matching of corresponding formulas, so don’t think about it in vain. Other real consumption formulas cannot match the keys of virtual items. After the corresponding formula is completed, the corresponding virtual items will be destroyed (actual items in the network will not be consumed and destroyed without any impact). The return function of the sample assembly is invalid for virtual items, and no actual items will be sent to the network."
				""
				"&74. You can place an order request when the physical virtual item is actually missing. The physical item will be returned to you and will not be swallowed up, but the virtual part will still be destroyed. When placing an order, the virtual item will display a purple field \"Virtual Presence\" to identify which requests contain virtual items."
				""
				"&cNote: The virtual item provider actually only identifies the corresponding templates that need the help of the virtual item system in the template code. Most of the time, the provider is only used to remind players which systems have virtual item systems and which do not. Don’t be like an idiot and get a virtual item provider bound to the corresponding item and just say why it can’t be used. Do you think you can get it for free? You can’t just grab a bundled virtual item provider and order something you don’t have."
			]
			id: "1CFDB2996A437B7F"
			optional: true
			quest_enhance_disable_scroll_paging: false
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "603C1454C959466D"
					item: "gt_shanhai:virtual_item_provider"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "2CEB920330D45FB5"
					item: "gt_shanhai:virtual_item_supply_machine"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "virtual item system"
			x: -9.5d
			y: 1.0d
		}
