		{
			description: [
				"&a&lneeds to be bound to the Forge of the False God. Use the hypertemporal data module to right-click the False God host."
				""
				"&bHypertime boost engine is a necessary module for opening gate control. If not, the gain will never take effect. &ais required."
				""
				"&bcatalytic stacking array provides a 2x output multiplier for the bound host. It also comes with an additional 0.15x eu reduction. &ais required."
				""
				"&bSpace-time stasis device stagnates the running time of the false god. The running time is no longer deducted when the false god is shut down. &dThe hub is locked and runs for 114514h."
				""
				"&bmagnetic flow convergence core Converts multiple fluid outputs into the total output of the first fluid &czone is useless"
				""
				"&cis also a required item for the Star Ceremony. Requirements:"
				"&erecursive inversion array gate control is in valid state"
				"&eThe hyperspace boost engine is running, not overheated, and in the optimal temperature range of 9.3wK-9.7wK"
				"If &l&cis satisfied, the star ceremony can be started. Otherwise, the star ceremony will not be started."
				"&7(Star Ritual, also known as Creation Box Recipe, is the only way for gtladditions to obtain Creation Boxes)"
				""
				"&a&l###gt_shanhai configuration file"
				"&6bypassModuleRestrictions &dWhether the recursive inversion array breaks the internal restrictions of the connected submodule (disabled by default)"
				"&cfalse=Keep the original logic of GTLAdditions: catalyst, focusing material, temperature window, and module operating status are all checked normally."
				"&atrue=Only when the sub-module has been formed and connected to the recursive inversion array, it will be regarded as full and participate in the recursive inversion gain. This configuration will not allow modules that run independently from the array to participate in the recursive inversion gain."
			]
			id: "1AC97F7D63F133C2"
			quest_enhance_disable_scroll_paging: false
			subtitle: "Recursive inversion array module"
			tasks: [
